The '''Mega Evolution Pokédex Shorts''' are a series of animated shorts that introduce mostly [[Mega Evolution|Mega-Evolved]] Pokémon that debuted in {{g|Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire}}.

In the original Japanese version, it originally aired as a post-credits segment of ''[[Pokémon the Series: XY]]'' in the place of [[Professor Oak's Pokémon Holo Caster]]. It aired from ''[[XY042|Battling Into the Hall of Fame!]]'' to ''[[XY054|Facing the Grand Design!]]'' (including the delayed ''[[XY024|An Undersea Place to Call Home!]]'').

In the English [[dub]], these segments were aired separately on the [[Pokémon TV]] service in {{pmin|the United States}}. Two were also uploaded to the official Pokémon YouTube channel.

==Structure==
The '''Mairin's Mega Evolution Journal''' (Japanese: '''マノンのメガシンカ絵日記''' ''{{tt|Manon|Mairin}}'s Mega Evolution Journal'') shorts feature {{wp|Chibi (term)|chibi}} versions of [[Mairin]] and [[Chespie]] as they present the shorts, providing commentary. Usually, [[Alain]] and his {{me|Charizard}} X join in and co-commentate. These Pokémon are often ones that Alain and Charizard fought during their journey.

Sometimes, {{Steven}} appears to present Mega Evolution Pokédex Shorts instead of Mairin. Steven's (Japanese: '''メガシンカ図鑑''' ''Mega Evolution Encyclopedia'') and (Japanese: '''ゲンシカイキの謎''' ''The Mysteries of Primal Reversion'') lectures feature [[Legendary Pokémon]], such as Mega {{p|Latias}} and {{p|Latios}}. [[XY044]] and [[XY054]]'s Mega Evolution Encyclopedia lectures were provided by the [[Lysandre|narrator]] of the [[Mega Evolution Specials]].

